// contract: modules.no-prelude
// status: preserve
// rationale: The language has no implicit prelude: without an import even `print`
//    is undeclared. Scripts start with `use "@core"` (or `@std`, which imports it).
//    Interactive hosts (the REPL, `flow -e`, `flow eval`) import @std themselves.
// errors: 1
// stderr: print
Int x = 5
(print "hi")
